course: dictionary
lesson: 10885
title: The viola
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The viola is a string instrument. It looks like a violin but is a little bigger, so it has a deeper, warmer sound. You play it with a bow and hold it under your chin.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. «Picture a family photo of strings: violin, viola, cello and double bass, from small to huge» shows that the viola belongs to the string family, between the violin and the cello.
explain: The word viola can also mean a small garden flower, like a pansy, or a girl's name. Look at the words around it. If the sentence talks about bows, notes and playing, it means the instrument.
fact: A viola is a string instrument played with a bow.
fact: «The violin, viola, cello and double bass are all string instruments played with a bow or plucked.»
fact: From highest to lowest, the string family is violin, viola, cello and double bass.
fact: «Viola» can also mean a small garden flower, like a little pansy.
fact: Viola is also a girl's name, as in Shakespeare's «Twelfth Night».
exercise: «In the string family bigger instruments play lower: from highest to lowest they are violin, viola, cello and double bass.» Which instrument plays lower than the violin? | *Viola | Recorder | Drum
exercise: What is the main difference between a viola and a violin? | *A little bigger, with a deeper, warmer sound | Played by blowing into it | Smaller and higher | The same size as a double bass
exercise: In a story about a garden, «viola» means what? | *A small flower, like a little pansy | A bow for playing | A string instrument | A large cello
test: «The cello and double bass are so big that they stand on the floor instead of resting under the chin like a violin.» Why don't cellos rest under the chin? | They prefer to stand | *They are too big to rest under the chin | They are played only by children | They are made of paper
test: Which sound is deeper, the viola or the violin? | Both are flowers | Neither, they are the same | Violin | *The viola
exam: «Picture a family photo of strings: violin, viola, cello and double bass, from small to huge.» Which instrument is the lowest in the string family? | Cello | Viola | Violin | *Double bass
